From d41ba60fada58cd98bc3cf1b07cc4b929003b2a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 09:49:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build item 3-8a's dual-representation local, and measure it

Off by default (BROILER_JS_SPECULATIVE_NUMERIC_LOCALS=1). A speculative
local is held as a raw double, a bool saying the double is live, and the
ordinary JSValue slot. Expression becomes a conditional over the two, so
every existing read site is correct without being touched and a write
through it is an assignment to a conditional, which the backend rejects
loudly rather than miscompiling -- the numeric tier's own safety
argument, reused. It deliberately does NOT get NumericStorage: five fast
paths read that field on the understanding that the binding IS a double,
and a speculative one is a double only sometimes.

Writes land the value in the slot, derive the flag from it and mirror
the raw half, branch-free, reading the flag and the double off the slot
rather than off the expression so a value with a side effect cannot run
twice. The paths that want the binding as an ordinary assignable JSValue
-- a compound assignment, a `with` fallback, a lexical initializer -- go
through one escape hatch that materializes the slot, writes in place and
resynchronizes. The ++/-- step branches on the flag, and while it holds
the increment is a native double add that writes nothing back to the
slot, which is the box the update-target census priced.

Measured on the corpus, one build, the switch the only difference: it
removes 835 584 update steps and ADDS 669 507 boxes. NavierStokes
1.057x, the corpus 1.021x. The mechanism does what it was built to do
and the reads pay for it twice over -- about 1.5 M boxes appear on
Expression's boxing arm, because while the raw half is live every read
that cannot consume a raw double has to mint one, and the shape reads
currentRow far more often than it increments it.

So the two consuming read paths are the rest of the item, and neither is
built: 0084's guarded arithmetic tree already carries exactly the right
leaf shape -- a raw double, a flag and a fallback value are what its
OrderedNode is -- and item 3-0's GetElementByNumber(double) already
takes a raw double as an index.

The arm also corrects the population count's own reading. The 15 names
carry 835 584 of NavierStokes' 9.46 M steps, 8.8%, not the whole of it:
the suite that holds the names being the suite that holds the traffic is
not the same claim as the names holding the traffic, and only running
the arm distinguishes them.

Shipped as a correct mechanism with its consumer missing, which is where
item 4-3b landed. 1 171 compiler, 4 571 integration, 2 103 built-ins,
11 runtime and 32 core tests green on BOTH settings, with
NumericLocalDefeatTests' four shape fixtures now Theories over the
switch: the answer is unchanged and only the row moves, LocalSlot when
off and nothing when on.
